+# CONTRACT — Constraint-Based Event Scheduler
+
+The `schedule(events, rooms, options)` function returns `{ assignments, unscheduled }`.
+
+## API surface
+- [ ] `schedule` is exported as a named export → import `{ schedule }` works
+- [ ] `schedule` is the default export → `import schedule from` works
+- [ ] `createScheduler()` factory returns an object with a `schedule` method
+- [ ] `Scheduler` class can be instantiated and has a `schedule` method
+- [ ] All types (`Event`, `Room`, `ScheduleOptions`, `Assignment`, `ScheduleResult`) are exported
+- [ ] `src/index.ts` re-exports everything from `src/scheduler.ts`
+
+## Core scheduling correctness
+- [ ] Single event fits in a room within the window → one assignment, start>=startTime, end<=endTime, end-start==duration
+- [ ] Assignment uses a room whose capacity >= attendees
+- [ ] attendees defaults to 1 when omitted
+- [ ] gap defaults to 15 when omitted
+
+## Rule 1: Room capacity
+- [ ] Event with attendees > every room capacity → unscheduled, no assignment
+- [ ] Event placed only in a room with capacity >= attendees (never an over-capacity room)
+- [ ] With multiple rooms, an event with large attendees goes into a room big enough
+
+## Rule 2: Time window
+- [ ] Every assignment has startTime >= options.startTime and endTime <= options.endTime
+- [ ] Event whose duration > (endTime - startTime) → unscheduled
+- [ ] Event ending exactly at endTime is allowed (end == endTime is valid)
+
+## Rule 3: Room gaps
+- [ ] Two events in the same room are separated by at least `gap` minutes (next.start - prev.end >= gap)
+- [ ] A custom gap value is respected
+- [ ] gap=0 allows back-to-back events in the same room
+- [ ] Events in DIFFERENT rooms need no gap between them (may overlap in time)
+
+## Rule 4: Prerequisites
+- [ ] If B requires A, then A.endTime + gap <= B.startTime (when both scheduled)
+- [ ] Prerequisite ordering holds even when A and B are in different rooms
+- [ ] If a prerequisite cannot be scheduled, the dependent event is also unscheduled
+- [ ] A prerequisite referencing an unknown event id → dependent unscheduled (no throw)
+- [ ] Chain A->B->C is ordered correctly with gaps
+
+## Rule 5: Preferred room
+- [ ] When preferredRoom is set and feasible, the event is placed in that room
+- [ ] preferredRoom is a hint: if it can't be honored, the event still gets scheduled elsewhere when possible
+- [ ] preferredRoom referencing an unknown room is ignored (event still scheduled)
+
+## Rule 6: Cycle detection (throws)
+- [ ] Self-reference A->A throws an Error
+- [ ] Two-node cycle A->B->A throws an Error
+- [ ] Larger cycle A->B->C->A throws an Error
+- [ ] A valid DAG does NOT throw
+
+## Rule 7 / Behavior: Maximize scheduled count
+- [ ] When not all events fit, the result maximizes number scheduled (beats naive in-order placement on a crafted case)
+- [ ] Events that cannot be placed appear in `unscheduled` (no throw)
+- [ ] Every event id appears exactly once across assignments + unscheduled (partition, no dupes/omissions)
+- [ ] Empty events list → empty assignments, empty unscheduled
+- [ ] No two assignments for the same event id
+
+## Invariants verified on every result (property checks)
+- [ ] No two events in the same room violate the gap
+- [ ] All capacity, window, prerequisite constraints hold for every assignment returned
+
+## Build / lint
+- [ ] `npm run build` compiles with no errors
+- [ ] `npm run lint` passes with no errors
+- [ ] `npm test` all tests pass
